# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is git-ignored — never commit keys.
# The same variables must also be set in Vercel:
#   Project → Settings → Environment Variables

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — required
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxx

# Server-only. Bypasses row-level security — never expose to the browser,
# never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Required to send waitlist invitations from
# the admin console (Supabase → Project Settings → API → service_role), and
# later for Stripe webhooks. Without it the Invite button explains what to set.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Signup protection — Cloudflare Turnstile
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional but strongly recommended. Without it the request form will accept
# anything a script posts at it. That is far less damaging than it used to be
# — a request creates no account and sends no email — but it still fills the
# review queue with rubbish.
#
#   1. Cloudflare → Turnstile → add a site → copy the site key and secret
#   2. Supabase → Authentication → Attack Protection → CAPTCHA → choose
#      Turnstile and paste the secret there too (that covers the sign-in form)
#   3. Put both keys below, and in Vercel. Never commit real values.
#
# Leave both unset and the challenge simply doesn't render — nothing breaks.
# The site key is public and renders the widget; the secret verifies the answer
# server-side in app/api/waitlist/route.ts, which is the half that matters.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Email sending — Resend, configured in the Supabase dashboard
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to set here. Invitations and sign-in links are sent by Supabase
# Auth, and it must NOT use its default shared sender: that address is shared
# by thousands of projects, lands in junk, and is limited to a few emails an
# hour. Supabase → Authentication → Emails → SMTP Settings points at
# smtp.resend.com (port 465, user "resend", password = a Resend API key) with
# hello@standoutwheneveryouspeak.com as the sender, and the domain is verified
# in Resend with the DNS records it lists. The invite wording lives in
# Advoc(Motiv)8/Invite-Email-Template.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Lesson video hosting
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave unset locally: videos are served from public/videos/ (git-ignored).
# Set in Vercel once videos are uploaded to a host. No trailing slash.
#
# UNSET IN PRODUCTION MEANS EVERY LESSON VIDEO 404s. The player now says so
# honestly rather than showing a black box, but the recordings still need a
# home. They are 1.13 GB, which does not fit Supabase's 1 GB free tier, and
# a single full course watch is 1.13 GB against 5 GB of monthly egress.
# scripts/upload-lesson-videos.mjs handles the upload and will tell you the
# exact value to paste here.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VIDEO_BASE_URL=https://your-host/lesson-videos

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe (not yet wired up)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI — Katya, the practice coach
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# One key serves the text sessions today and the voice coach later. Without
# it the topic workspace still saves a member's Frame and Masterful Notes;
# starting a session says "Katya isn't connected yet" and points here.
# Katya's instructions are Barry's context prompt (lib/katya-context.ts).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# Optional — the chat model for text sessions. Defaults to gpt-5-mini.
# OPENAI_TEXT_MODEL=gpt-5-mini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin insight agent
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Required for the Insights panel in the admin console.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# Optional — defaults to gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
